 13	 *     protocol with `gc_grace` retention. `purgeMedia` below no longer
 14	 *     deletes blob bytes itself — after removing the media row it only
 15	 *     triggers the tombstone-pass (`tombstoneBlobIfUnreferenced`); actual
 16	 *     byte removal is deferred to `runBlobGcDeletePass` +
 17	 *     `runBlobGcUnlinkPass` (or the `runBlobGcCycle` convenience wrapper),
 18	 *     which nothing in this repo schedules automatically yet (no scheduler
 19	 *     exists — see `blob-gc.ts`'s file header). `uploadMedia`'s dedup check
 20	 *     is likewise serialized per-sha256 and resurrects a tombstoned blob
 21	 *     instead of writing a duplicate. See `blob-gc.ts` for what's still
 22	 *     disclosed-stubbed within that protocol (`entry_refs`, retained
 23	 *     snapshots, the monthly orphan sweep).
 24	 *  2. **Named transform registry / real image processing** — the only
 25	 *     rendition this build ever creates is a trivial "original" passthrough
 26	 *     row that points at the source blob (created by `uploadMedia`). No
